  "body": "Reportedly, and I think https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/8561 demonstrates this but not entirely due to different task sources, the `</svg>` end tag (when it pops an `<svg>` element from the stack), queues a task to dispatch a `load` event on that element, in both the HTML and XML parser.\r\n\r\nThis is not really defined and since it's a thing in the parsers, it should be defined in HTML.\r\n\r\nOther tests:\r\n* https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/8565\r\n* `<svg onload=w(1)><image href=image onload=w(2)></svg>` (2, then 1 in Chrome/Safari; just 1 in Firefox). This shows actually defining this might be somewhat involved and would need cooperation from the SVG WG.\r\n\r\ncc @AmeliaBR ",
